<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="TAM 335" href="schedule/2005/spring/TAM/335.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2005" href="schedule/2005.xml">2005</calendarYear><term id="120051" href="schedule/2005/spring.xml">Spring 2005</term><subject id="TAM" href="schedule/2005/spring/TAM.xml">Theoretical and Applied Mechanics</subject></parents><label>Introductory Fluid Mechanics</label><description>(T A M 235) Fluid statics; continuity, momentum and energy principles via control volumes; ideal and real fluid flow; introduction to the Navier Stokes equation; similitude; laminar and turbulent boundary layers; closed-conduit flow, open-channel flow, and turbomachinery. Lecture/lab format.  Prerequisite: TAM 212. </description><creditHours>4 hours.</creditHours><sections><section id="36262" href="schedule/2005/spring/TAM/335/36262.xml">AB1</section><section id="36263" href="schedule/2005/spring/TAM/335/36263.xml">AB2</section><section id="36264" href="schedule/2005/spring/TAM/335/36264.xml">AB3</section><section id="36265" href="schedule/2005/spring/TAM/335/36265.xml">AB4</section><section id="36266" href="schedule/2005/spring/TAM/335/36266.xml">AB5</section><section id="36267" href="schedule/2005/spring/TAM/335/36267.xml">AE1</section></sections></ns2:course>